<!--Post: 7722--><!--Time: 1108665733-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7722"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Neechi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Neechi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 10:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->All of this is just musings from my mind, I&#39;m not an expert or professional, but I thought I would share my theory and see what ya&#39;ll think. <BR> <BR>Ken Landwehr mentioned in an interview, that BTK might have experienced trauma as a child and it got me thinking that maybe BTK was &#34;growing up&#34; as a killer through his crimes, bear with me here. <BR> <BR>If you accept that Josephine Otero was the targeted victim for BTK, that would kind of represent the pre-adolescent puppy love stage of development &#40;the other killings were only necessary to reach his goal&#41;.  Then he moves on to the still young Bright woman, not married no kids, just good college fun.  Then Vian, no longer needing to fulfill his childhood fantasy, he only kills the young mother.  Symbolizing the idea of settling down and having a family.  But BTK soon tires of the routine and monotony, so he goes on to an &#34;affair&#34; with Nancy Fox, then settles down with Vicki Wegerle.   <BR> <BR>Now recent media speculation has wondered if there is a connection to the Davis homicide, if she was in fact a victim, you could put that down as the passing of a loved one.  Now he is informing his &#34;children and grandchildren&#34; &#40;the media, the police&#41; of his life and activities and passing down our inheritance. <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t know that this theory holds any water, but my little brain thought it interesting...thanks for reading!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7722-->
<!--Post: 7732--><!--Time: 1108667508-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7732"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 11:11 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Interesting idea Neechi, and who knows what strange patterns lay under BTK´s acts, yours could be as right as any other of the theories around here. <BR> <BR>Adding to you theorie: Anna Williams &#40;intended victim who was out dancing till late, wich saved her life BTK tired of waiting,poem: &#34;Oh Anna why didn´t you appear?&#34;&#41; could symbolize the woman a man grow old with? <BR> <BR>welcome to the forum...skov<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7732-->
<!--Post: 7735--><!--Time: 1108668360-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7735"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Neechi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Neechi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 11:26 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks for the warm welcome Skov!  Anna Williams was a hard one to figure out for my theory, since the police seem to think that he was actually targeting the woman&#39;s daughter.  I guess I could chalk her up as the .&#34;one that got away&#34;...unrequited love type of thing.  I guess we won&#39;t know until he publishes his &#34;book&#34;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7735-->
<!--Post: 7790--><!--Time: 1108683985-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7790"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 3:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK&#39;s victim choices are one of the most peculiar things about his crimes.  There seems to be something weird and Freudian about the Otero crime especially.  It would be great to know what his actual family background is, including any siblings he may have.   We&#39;ll just have to wait and see what we find out if/when he&#39;s caught. <BR> <BR>Some serial killers don&#39;t seem to have any special targets, they&#39;re just homicidal maniacs -- Peter Kurten &#40;sp?&#41; was a German serial killer who killed men, women, children, just about anyone unfortunate enough to run into him on a lonely, dark street.  He even killed animals -- he killed some swans that were in a public park.  What a kook.  Maybe BTK is more in that vein.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7790-->
<!--Post: 7798--><!--Time: 1108686180-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7798"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 4:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Neechi, that is an interesting theory but I don&#39;t think they were planned out to be that way. <BR> I think they were random killings but maybe in his subliminal mind he was doing just that as you have described without even realizing it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7798-->
<!--Post: 7800--><!--Time: 1108686298-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7800"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:nugzter@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 4:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Audreyamw, <BR>I agree with you I have made posts on this topic befoe. Just search nugzter and look fo animal torture. also search for horses. <BR> Alot of seial killers start in ealy years on animals. I think there is a horse killing connection. It is a common occurance in rual areas. Most conspirace theorists say its aliens that kill the horses. But for LE flags should go up, it is something like a build up to humans.  <BR>I saw a documentary on German sexual serial killers, and one guy would slowly kill the horse he bound, he slit it open and cawled inside and had sex with the guts. He was 20 something, a few years later he graduated to women. He was caught quickly thank God. But it as avenue to look into.  <BR>Again I ask the question, <BR>Were there any horse or possably cow killings in the 60&#39;s or 70&#39;s aound the area?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7800-->
